<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="052" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Extend MetricCard, DocumentRowMenu and OutcomeCard rather than rebuilding</title>
    <phase>5 The worklist surface</phase>
    <gate>051 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Component-reuse rule is binding; building past a named existing component is a section 11 violation.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Extension of three identified components with known file and line references.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>051</deps>
    <tags>frontend,fluent-ui,reuse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Extend the three named shipped components for count filters, the row menu and the post-action outcome surface. Do not build parallel ones.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE front-end developer. Default to reuse; new surface needs a justification it cannot give here.</role>
  <goal>Count filters, the row menu and the outcome surface all come from extended shipped components.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>The reuse audit found three components that would otherwise be rebuilt, each with a named file and line range. Building past them is a CLAUDE.md section 11 violation with no cost-of-doing-nothing to cite.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/MetricCard.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentRowMenu.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkChat/OutcomeCard.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: count-filter cards extend WorkspaceShell/MetricCard.tsx:24-222 plus MetricCardRow. They are ALREADY clickable (role=button), square and badge-capable. Do NOT use StatTiles, which has NO onClick at all (StatTiles.tsx:95-111) and carries the overlapping-lenses semantics being retired.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the row menu extends DocumentRowMenu.tsx:150-208, an action-descriptor table with disabledActions filtering. Do NOT hand-roll a fourth menu: three bespoke ones already exist (DocumentRowMenu, NarrativeBullet.tsx:600-645, HighPrioritySection.tsx:298-325), which is section 11 own named anti-pattern.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the post-action surface extends SprkChat/OutcomeCard.tsx:93-367, already status badge plus summary plus link plus next-step chips. Add the Signal statuses; do not build a parallel worklist outcome card.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: ALWAYS cite the full path for MetricCard. A second unrelated one exists at Spaarke.Visuals/src/components/MetricCard.tsx (task 011 disambiguated this).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: count filters are LENSES ON MEMBERSHIP, not separate queues. Clicking one filters the existing list; it does not open another list.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Scope: Fluent v9 tokens only across all three extensions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: C-9 (assigned here 2026-10-03). Extract a shared RowActionMenu from DocumentRowMenu, build the worklist row against it, and migrate the four other hand-rolled row menus onto it.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Component reuse and extension</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/standards/ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/COMPONENT-COMPLEXITY.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/BUILD-A-NEW-WORKSPACE-WIDGET.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKEAI-DASHBOARD-AND-WIDGET-MODEL.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/reuse-verification-2026-10-02.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code.</step>
    <step order="1">Read each of the three components and record what it already does, so the extension is additive.</step>
    <step order="2">Extend MetricCard or MetricCardRow for the lane count filters, preserving the existing clickable behavior.</step>
    <step order="3">Extend DocumentRowMenu with the Work Item action descriptors, reusing its disabledActions filtering.</step>
    <step order="4">Extend OutcomeCard with the Signal statuses (complete, reschedule, reassign, dismiss).</step>
    <step order="5">Add tests for each extension and confirm no existing consumer regressed.</step>
    <step order="6">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="7">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any of the three genuinely cannot be extended, STOP and escalate with the specific blocking reason. The reuse rule is binding, and a new parallel component needs owner sign-off rather than an implementer decision.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Count filters act as lenses">
      <steps>
        <step>Render the worklist with lane count filters</step>
        <step>Click a count filter</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The existing list filters in place; no second list or queue opens.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Row menu reuses the descriptor table">
      <steps>
        <step>Open the row menu on a Work Item with one unavailable action</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The unavailable action is filtered out by disabledActions, not hidden by bespoke logic.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Outcome card shows Signal statuses">
      <steps>
        <step>Complete a Work Item</step>
        <step>Observe the outcome surface</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>OutcomeCard renders the new status with its summary and next-step chips.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode compliance per ADR-021">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode</step>
        <step>Exercise all three extensions</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All three adapt via semantic tokens.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build and test the shared UI package</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/MetricCard.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentRowMenu.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkChat/OutcomeCard.tsx</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the worklist count filters, when inspected, then they are MetricCard or MetricCardRow instances, not new components and not StatTiles.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the row menu, when inspected, then it is DocumentRowMenu with added action descriptors, and the repo still contains no fourth bespoke menu.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the post-action surface, when inspected, then it is OutcomeCard extended with Signal statuses.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: clicking a count filter filters the existing list and does not open a second queue.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no existing consumer of any of the three components regressed; their existing tests pass unmodified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The package builds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">One shared RowActionMenu exists, extracted from DocumentRowMenu; the worklist row and the four former row menus all use it.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-27. design.md section 1.3 is BINDING, not advisory.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
